## Exercises *exercises*

Try these exercises to practice what you've learned.

### Exercise 1: Flash Jump

Look at this line of text:

~~~
The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
~~~

Press `s` then the letter `o` to trigger Flash labels, then type the
label shown on the `o` in `fox` to jump there.

✗ Press `s` then `o` then the label on `fox`

### Exercise 2: Multicursor

Move to the word `foo` below and press `<leader>n` three times to
select all three occurrences, then press `ciwbar<Esc>` to change them
all to `bar`:

~~~
foo bar foo baz foo qux
~~~

✗ `<leader>n` x3 then `ciwbar<Esc>`

### Exercise 3: Code Folding

Place your cursor on the function below and press `zM` to close all
folds, then press `zR` to open them again:

~~~python
def hello():
    print("hello")
    print("world")
~~~

✗ `zM` to close folds, then `zR` to open all folds

